    "content": [
      {
        "type": "thinking",
        "thinking": "I'm trying to recall whether कुण (आमन्त्रणे) belongs to the curadi class and whether it's listed among the ātmanepadī exceptions in that gana, thinking through the traditional sutra enumerating those roots like चित, दसि, and others.\n\nI'm trying to recall whether \"कुण आमन्त्रणे\" appears in curadi or if it's actually \"कुण शब्दोपकरणयोः\" from tudadi, since these invitation/calling roots seem to cluster near \"ग्राम आमन्त्रणे\" and \"केत श्रावणे निमन्त्रणे\" in the kathādi group rather than curadi proper.\n\nContinuing through the list of curadi roots, I confirm कुण fits among the अदन्त, ubhayapada curadi verbs taking णिच् like गुण, सङ्केत, and केत, all meaning invitation or summoning.\n\nSo कुण falls in कथादि group, ubhayapadi via णिचश्च. For āśīrliṅ kartari, I'll go with parasmaipada using यासुट्, applying णि-lopa since यासुट् is कित् and अनिट्: कुण (अदन्त) + णिच् loses its final अ, giving कुण्.\n\nSince the lopa is sthānivat (अचः परस्मिन्पूर्वविधौ), it blocks upadhā guṇa, giving कुणयति for the causative. For āśīrliṅ uttama bahuvacana parasmaipada, कुणि + यास्म, then णेरनिटि removes the णि, yielding the final answer कुण्यास्म.\n\n",
        "signature": ""
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<answer>कुण्यास्म</answer>"
      }
